from core import EXTRACT_PROMPT

PROMPT_V3=EXTRACT_PROMPT+'''
Clarifications of the ontology (apply to all sources):
1. Commitment is normative for a prescription/recommendation: should, must, ought, need to do an ACTION. Epistemic 'must be true' is certain, not normative. Explicit might/may/could/possibly is possible; probably/likely/seems reasonable is probable. A statement that an alleged justification does not follow is a descriptive/evaluative denial (certain unless qualified), even if it mentions someone else's recommendation. For a merely reported argument, annotate the strength of its reported conclusion, not the reporter's confidence.
2. Stance is toward the WARRANT being evaluated. An author rejecting a reported causal chain, alleged expert justification, popularity inference or exhaustive choice restriction is critiques, even though the author actively uses a rebuttal. Merely listing other options is uses with alternatives=open. Explicitly saying a claimed restriction is false is critiques with alternatives=denied; denied takes precedence over open when both occur. Include grounded challenged/reported reasoning instead of dropping it just because it is not endorsed.
3. Natural_property means appeal to natural ORIGIN/NORMALITY as justification of value, acceptability or how we ought to act. Ordinary physical cause-and-effect involving a natural property is causal_projection/evidence, not a value-from-nature warrant.
4. For explicit priority/severity comparisons used to prioritize an action, priority_comparison is the main warrant even if a limited budget creates a choice. A genuine physical exhaustive set (such as a two-position switch) can use alternatives; the operator is neutral and does not assert a fallacy. An open choice list can justify exploring more options.
5. Preserve the strongest central claim, not all clauses in sequence. An evaluation described in order to rebut it is not an author's premise for the author's own conclusion. Separate distinct reasoning moves only when both are explicitly grounded.
Do not name or predict fallacy classes. Keep all original contract fields.'''

PROMPT_V4=PROMPT_V3+'''
The input units now include shorter clauses, not always standalone assertions. Read their original context before assigning premise/conclusion roles. Quoted content and conditionals remain quoted/hypothetical; an evidence unit is not automatically an asserted fact.
Cover each DISTINCT explicitly grounded central warrant, up to four. If an action is advocated through BOTH a consequence projection and an exhaustive choice restriction, preserve both reasoning moves with their respective premise/conclusion anchors. An explicit 'only option', 'either ... or', or 'nothing else' restriction may be in the conclusion, not only in the premise. Do not omit such a restriction just because the justification also mentions harms. For each alternatives move set closed/open/denied according to the source.
If a clause says a limited observation 'shows/means/proves' a much broader property, inspect those split clauses for generalization instead of automatically treating them as a causal forecast. Use broader only when source and target scopes actually expand.
For a projected chain, record the actual ordered event-clause IDs, not rhetorical questions or the final policy recommendation. If two events remain inside one unsplit unit, do not invent an extra event ID.
Do not add a warrant just because its keyword occurs. Named politicians or organizations are not testimony unless their status or statements are used as justification. Likewise, a democratic rule can be reasonable even when a consensus-related warrant is present.
Return the same exact JSON contract.'''

PROMPT_V6=PROMPT_V4+'''
Units have now been segmented into atomic source spans. Their envelope preserves the parent clause. Use separate observed-sample and broader-target units when a conditional or inference was embedded in one sentence. Do not mistake the fact that a conclusion is a prediction for an explicit causal mechanism.
Generalization includes cross-PROPERTY or cross-DOMAIN extrapolation about the same actor/group: failure in one task -> assumed incompetence in all tasks; observing one aspect of a society -> predicting its unrelated attributes; a few participants' passion -> assuming the wider population is equally passionate. It can be hedged ('probably', 'would not surprise me') and still be broader. Use the actual observed-property unit as premise, not an intervening 'therefore it is legitimate' conclusion. By contrast, causal_projection needs a proposed event/process leading to another event, not merely an unobserved property assigned to a group.
When an author explicitly questions/rejects a reported unsupported attribution or restricted inference, retain that challenged reasoning with stance=critiques if its relevant premise and conclusion can be grounded. Do not invent a broader population if the issue is only an alternative causal explanation.
Do not give consensus merely because the subject is people. Consensus needs beliefs, popularity, group choice or participation used AS the justification. Generic criticism of people is evidence/other, not popularity as warrant.
Return the unchanged exact argument JSON contract.'''

PROMPT_V8=PROMPT_V6+'''
Titles inform what pronouns/issues refer to but are not independent comment-author conclusions. Do not add an argument just to use every title/context unit. Omit unsupported extra reasoning moves.
For replies: explicit agreement with a parent ('makes sense', 'you are right', 'I agree') can adopt parts of its reasoning. Retain only the parent links actually adopted by the comment, with the comment's qualification: 'a reasonable possibility' does not inherit an inevitable/certain outcome. The comment's own qualified risk may justify its own recommendation. Refuted or merely reported parent links remain critiques/reports, never automatically uses. Use parent anchors only where this relationship is actually supported.
When event units separately state an initial action and its 'will lead to' consequence, retain their actual ordered IDs in chain even if there are only two stated events. Never add an event that does not have a real source unit.
Return at most four genuine grounded moves, not four merely because the cap is four.'''
